WEBVTT

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:27.950
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:27.950
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:27.950
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.530 --> 00:02:01.950
The Duelist
Chapter II

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:10.070
In January of Imperial Year 483, the
rumor that Lieutenant Reinhard von Musel...

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:13.880
...or rather, Countess 
Grunewald's younger brother...

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.050
...would represent Viscount
Schafhausen{Shakhausen} in a duel...

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.860
...spread around the aristocratic society of Odin in no time.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.530
Have you heard about the duel ?

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.480
I heard Countess Gruenwald's younger brother will try his best to pretend to fight a duel.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:36.250
Well, even though he's an aristocrat,
he's only a <i>Reichsritter</i>, after all.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.000
Such low-bred behavior
is quite appropriate for him.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:41.280
Indeed, indeed.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.730
Oh, speak of the devil.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.350
One of the involved
parties has just appeared.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.410
Well, let's hear his story, shall we ?

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.140
Count - Count Helksheimer !

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.550
Oh, you're all here.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.800
How are you ?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:04.700
How are you ?

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.980
I heard, I heard.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.160
Count, it sounds like something
interesting is happening.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.160
Oh no, it was so unexpected.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.150
I'm astonished that it has
become such a big event.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.300
But now this duel is the
target of a lot of attention.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.720
I'm looking forward to it.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:38.240
Well, since the opponent is an
amateur kid, the outcome is too obvious.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.680
It's not worth your attention.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.160
So you say, but your
agent is first-class, isn't he ?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.800
Well, of course.
It's a matter of pride, you see.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.750
Since ancient days, we've said lions exert maximum effort even when they're just hunting a little rabbit.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.910
We won't let our guard down.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.470
Then it won't be much of a gamble.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.310
That's disappointing.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.300
But as a show, it could be interesting.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.950
Well, we'll do our best to ensure all the fine
points of honor and ceremony are observed...

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.050
...so please do expect a good show.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.280
What ? That brat will...?

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.580
Call Glaser.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.710
Immediately !

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:38.180
Basically, a duel must be carried out between two people of the same social class.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:41.540
For a duel between aristocrats,
their titular ranks are not an issue...

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.960
...but a duel between an aristocrat and a commoner is not permitted.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.400
Also, in the case of
active military personnel...

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:51.520
...a duel is permitted only between
two people of the same rank.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.450
If a superior and a subordinate fight in a duel, that would interfere with military tasks...

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.650
...and would make it difficult to uphold the spirit of a hierarchical society.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:03.700
There's a loophole; if one of them is retired, there'd be no problem.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:04.780
I see.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:10.270
But it seems none of these are an issue
if it's fought between the agents of aristocrats.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:13.460
Essentially, the ones dueling
are the aristocrats themselves...

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:16.460
...and the agents are
basically considered to be...

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:18.500
Huh ?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.750
...like objects.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.100
I'm an object ?

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.860
Please don't say that.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:35.150
But getting to the duel itself, 
what weapon am I expected to use ?

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:40.370
There seems to be many options, but basically, a pistol.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.290
And if the fight remains
unsettled, then a sword.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:49.840
And if the fight still remains unsettled, it seems it's on to bare hands.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.500
Bare hands ?

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:57.300
In reality, it seems that kind of fierce fight almost never takes place.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.950
In most cases, when one side robs the
other of his fighting ability with his pistol...

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:02.000
...the duel comes to an end.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:06.080
So it'll be pistols.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.950
As a matter of preference...

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.800
...sometimes a duel can be started with swords as the designated weapon.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.950
The weapon is usually determined
by the side that accepted the duel...

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.960
...so in this case,
it's our choice, but...

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.060
Then it'll be pistols.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.320
You might want to
wait before you decide.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.840
For a duel with pistols,
there are certain rules.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:32.440
In a duel of pistols, as Baroness Westpfahle explained it, the most reputable way to win...

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:37.510
...is to shoot down the opponent's pistol, 
and that requires the skill level of a master.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.980
You'd probably be able to do it.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:43.310
I don't know, I'm not that confident.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.390
You're being humble.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:49.040
In military preparatory school, your 
shooting skills were top in the class.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.770
That's not what I meant.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:51.980
There's a problem.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.390
"Problem" ?

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:57.950
I'll talk about it later, but the next
most reputable way to win a duel is...

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:02.610
...to shoot the opponent's arm, then shoulder, and then leg.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:05.240
To shoot the body is 
considered to be a "low" blow.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.790
Further, fatally injuring the opponent would be considered the lowest of the low...

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:12.080
...and even if you win the duel,
it'll be considered to be a disgrace.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.370
That's silly.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.300
Isn't winning the purpose
 of it, whatever you do ?

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:19.630
Lord Reinhard, you can't
use stones this time.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:23.440
I know.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.750
I probably should aim 
for the opponent's arm.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.220
I would think that would be the best.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.990
So, what was the "problem" ?

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.850
The pistol you'll be using
is not a blaster but rather...

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:34.350
Huh ?

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.390
...an old-fashioned pistol
that uses gunpowder.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.410
Gunpowder ?

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:42.450
It looks like this, but have
you ever used one before ?

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:46.520
No, I haven't.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.330
That's what I thought.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.950
Father, it's really loud.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.200
If you're amazed at
this volume of sound...

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.750
...you won't be able to go hunting
and shoot deer yourself.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:29.010
But, Darling, it sounds
louder than hunting rifles.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.670
Can't be.

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:33.520
For ladies, this might be a little crude.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.850
For the little lady, how about if I show her a pony over there ?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.410
Shall we, Sabine ?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.590
Yes, Mother.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:55.210
The duelist you've hired,
are you certain he's sure-handed ?

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:56.750
Yes, of course.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:01.780
I hired a master who has never lost in
any of the countless duels he's fought.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.650
By the way, I heard the
opponent has found a duelist.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.410
It's amazing that someone
actually accepted the role.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:22.580
Well, it seems the Schafhausens 
went crying to Countess Grunewald...

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.450
...and the Countess's younger brother...

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:28.500
...someone named Lieutenant Musel, accepted being their agent.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.290
What ?

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.410
That wench has a younger brother ?

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:36.040
Wait, the younger brother of 
that young wench, that means...

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:38.000
A brat of the age of 16, I heard.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.580
Well, if his sister is a planet that
revolves around the sun of the Kaiser...

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:46.580
...she has a satellite, so to speak.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:51.960
If he's just a satellite it would be better for him to just hide in the planet's shadow and stay quiet.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.950
Why would he bother
being so audacious ?

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.730
He's just conceited, I suppose.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:10:00.580
This is a good opportunity; we'll
teach him a painful lesson or two.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.100
That's good.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:08.000
Make him suffer a miserable defeat, and embarrass that wench{i.e. Annerose} as well.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.320
Marquis, it seems you
resent Countess Grunewald ?

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.790
Of course I do !

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:19.650
Think what'll happen if that
wench gives birth to a male child.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:22.450
The Kaiser will gladly
take him as his successor.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:29.330
If that happened, there would be no possibility that your daughter would be Kaiserin.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:34.030
Since the prince died young the blood-relations who are most likely to succeed to the throne...

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:40.500
...are limited to either my daughter Sabine or Braunschweig's Elizabeth.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:45.080
Since it is essentially settled that one of the two will succeed the throne as Kaiserin...

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:49.670
...I would hate it if anything happened to complicate the situation.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:55.370
It's the same as what happened with Marchioness Benemunde.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:58.610
At that time, a male 
child actually was born.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:02.030
It was stillborn.
He wasn't born.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:08.060
He was born safely, but a doctor who was
acting on someone's order actually killed him.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.750
There was some rumor
like that, wasn't there ?

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.070
It's a rumor without any foundation.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.810
I don't know anything about it.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:17.590
But Braunschweig might have done something like that.

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:26.160
At that time, too, if her male
child had been born safely...

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.140
...it was rumored that 
Marchioness Benemunde...

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:31.140
...would be given the 
position of a Kaiserin consort.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:32.200
In that regard...

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:38.780
...if Countess Grunewald gives birth to a successor, she will have the same chance, too.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:43.030
Marchioness Benemunde is from a legitimate viscount family.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:45.460
Her lineage is different
from that of the wench's.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:49.100
Even if that wench were
to be given such a chance...

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:52.500
...suppose all of us high aristocrats opposed such a move.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:56.100
The Kaiser would
certainly be dissuaded.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.450
Indeed.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.550
Besides, the Kaiser himself 
probably has no intention of the sort.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.970
The fact that the wench, even after six years of being in his harem...

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:11.100
...has never indicated conceiving a child is the evidence.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:19.550
My humble self is not able to 
discern His Majesty's intentions...

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:23.000
...but what your Excellency
says must be right.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:24.790
We've digressed.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:27.330
Getting back to the matter of the duel...

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:28.250
Yes.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:30.580
I would like to see it myself.

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:34.310
It would be an unexpected honor
to have you among the spectators.

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:37.530
You haven't chosen the
place yet, have you ?

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:38.320
Not yet.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.580
Then there's an appropriate
place inside my manor grounds.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:44.550
It would be easy
for me to watch there.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:46.830
I may borrow it ?

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.590
Yes, that'll be fine, fine.

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:50.300
I'll have my people make preparations.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:53.010
Thank you for such an honor.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:55.120
In return...

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:57.870
I understand.

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:04.530
When I obtain the mining rights, I will supply hydro-metal to the military through your hands.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:28.600
Splendid shot.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:29.790
It was so-so.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:42.080
It's rather heavy.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.100
Is it like this ?

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:50.090
In the actual duel, you'll hold one in 
each hand, and it'll be a two-shot fight.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:52.880
You might want to get accustomed to shooting one-handed.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:54.930
Like this ?

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.870
What a noise.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.040
Yeah, and it gets on my hand, too.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.500
On top of that,
I missed the mark, too.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.170
Well, it's hard to do on the first shot.

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:41.150
What's wrong with this pistol ?

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.150
Is the sight line distorted ?

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.000
It's not the pistol's fault.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.580
Sorry to interrupt you,
but I heard an interesting noise.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:25.030
Unlike a blaster or a beam rifle,
gunpowder firearms recoil.

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:29.550
Taking that into consideration, you'll do
better if you aim a little lower than the target.

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:31.060
Why don't you try ?

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:32.070
Y...yes.

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:45.300
A hit.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.730
Well, you seem to have the aptitude.

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:51.520
But the recoil is causing a slight
movement of the body when you shoot.

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:53.200
In order to minimize the movement...

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:57.300
...you should put your left arm in front of your body, and rest your right arm on it.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:58.240
Yeah, that's it.

00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.130
Shoot it like that.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.880
Well, you're good.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:09.580
Keep working on it.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:11.300
Um...

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:12.880
What is it ?

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:15.180
Thank you for the instruction.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:17.650
If you don't mind, I wonder if I may ask for your honorable name ?

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.450
I don't know if it's "honorable" ...

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:24.550
...but I'm Lutz, Cornelius Lutz.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:25.620
I am...

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:26.730
I know.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:28.160
You're Lieutenant Musel, right ?

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.550
You're famous.

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:45.900
Who is he ?

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.510
He's not my opponent
in the duel, is he ?

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:52.900
No, your opponent isn't
an active military officer.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.720
I've confirmed that.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:57.650
Then I wonder if 
he's simply a meddler.

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.300
He's interesting.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:06.350
To say that about someone older
than you, and a senior officer to boot...

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:07.720
...you're quite "interesting," too.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.700
You're getting the hang of it.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:15.770
Yeah.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:18.200
It looks like the weapon
of choice will be a pistol.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:35.720
I don't know who you are, 
but if you're hiding, come on out !

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:42.060
I, duelist Goltschmidt{ ?Goldschmidt ?}, have accepted your challenge and come for you !

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:56.040
You're the one who
sent the letter of challenge ?

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.500
I don't know what
grudge you may have...

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:05.360
...but as a duelist, I will not 
run away from a challenge.

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:09.350
I'm awaiting an important fight, but this will serve as a good warm-up.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.590
Which weapon do you want to use, a pistol or a sword ?

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:12.820
As you like.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.820
Then it'll be pistols.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.070
You have yours, I presume ?

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.580
Of course.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:18.920
We'll use one pistol.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.980
A one-shot fight should
be plenty, shouldn't it ?

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:24.170
We'll face in opposite directions, and fire after ten steps.

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.030
You have no complaint
about this format, I presume ?

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.330
I accept.

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.130
Then draw !

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:47.210
Now we'll commence.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:48.850
One !

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:51.600
Two !

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:54.700
Three !

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.650
Four !

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.500
Five !

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:03.200
Six !

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:06.200
Seven !

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:09.550
Eight !

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:12.550
Nine !

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.600
Ten !

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.340
You bastard...

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:05.090
...it's against the rules
to shoot in the chest.

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:09.010
I'm sorry.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:11.860
I'm not a duelist...

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.200
...I'm an assassin.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:27.940
What ?

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:29.820
Goltschmidt is dead ?

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:31.180
What happened ?

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:39.400
Master, there's a man at the door who says he'd like to be hired as a duelist.

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:40.950
What ?

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:05.330
As instructed, I've succeeded in sending our man to be the Helksheimers' duelist.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.570
That's good to know.

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:11.950
But make sure that his 
connection to me is kept secret.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.980
Yes, I know.

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:17.150
The rest is to make it seem like an accident in a duel...

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.740
And be prepared for the
unlikely case scenario as well.

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:21.510
Yes.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:25.400
In Captain Helder's case,
our secret was almost leaked...

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:28.780
...but this time I've made
preparations to "keep him quiet"{i.e. have another assassin ready to kill the assassin}.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:29.980
That's good.

00:21:29.980 --> 00:21:33.360
Now I have something
fun to look forward to.

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:52.240
Good.

00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:57.750
Master, are you sure ?

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.940
He may have shot Goltschmidt.

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:07.020
If that's the case, it means
he's the better duelist.

00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:12.760
He probably wants to become famous.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:15.090
If he's useful to me,
that's all that counts.

00:22:15.090 --> 00:22:17.300
I see.

00:22:17.950 --> 00:22:21.230
More importantly, did you
send the letter of challenge ?

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:23.090
Yes, certainly.

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:23.780
Good.

00:22:27.790 --> 00:22:28.700
Lord Reinhard.

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:34.510
The Helksheimers have designated the time and place for the duel.

00:22:36.780 --> 00:22:40.510
It was the letter of challenge in accordance with custom.

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:44.110
But at the same time, it was a letter of invitation to death.

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:47.500
At this point, neither
Reinhard nor Kircheis...

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:50.650
...were aware of the life-threatening danger that was awaiting him.

